:"Sonat ut Anglicum 'w' (ut in 'vīnum')"}],"explanation":"Distinctio inter vocalem et consonantem, et duplex valor litterarum I/V, fundamentum est totius pronuntiationis Latinae.","exerciseType":"matching","exerciseId":"i-alph-match","exerciseTitle":"Iunge Terminum cum Definitione","exerciseInstructions":"Iunge quemque terminum grammaticum cum definitione recta.","lessonId":"i-alphabetum-et-soni","lessonTitle":"Alphabetum et Soni","level":"I","lessonUrl":"gradus/fundamenta/alphabetum-et-soni.html"},"cons1":{"id":"cons1","prompt":"'C' in 'Cicero' pronuntiatur:","options":["[k] [k], ambae dure, ut Anglicum 'kite'","[s] [s], molliter","[tʃ] [tʃ], ut Italicum 'ciao'"],"answerIndex":0,"explanation":"C semper [k] in Latinitate Classica.","exerciseType":"multiple-choice","exerciseId":"i-cons-mc","exerciseTitle":"Consonantes: C, G, QU, S, TI","exerciseInstructions":"Elige responsum rectum.","lessonId":"i-consonantes","lessonTitle":"Consonantes","level":"I","lessonUrl":"gradus/fundamenta/consonantes.html"},"cons2":{"id":"cons2","prompt":"'G' in 'gemma' pronuntiatur:","options":["dure, ut Anglicum 'g' in 'go'","molliter, ut Anglicum 'j' in 'gem'","muta"],"answerIndex":0,"explanation":"G semper dura, numquam mollis in aetate classica.","exerciseType":"multiple-choice","exerciseId":"i-cons-mc","exerciseTitle":"Consonantes: C, G, QU, S, TI","exerciseInstructions":"Elige responsum rectum.","lessonId":"i-consonantes","lessonTitle":"Consonantes","level":"I","lessonUrl":"gradus/fundamenta/consonantes.html"},"cons3":{"id":"cons3","prompt":"'Qu' in verbo 'aqua' tractatur ut:","options":["consonans una labiovelaris [kʷ] cum vocali sequenti in eadem syllaba","duae consonantes in syllabis distinctis (a-ku-a)","vocalis, non consonans"],"answerIndex":0,"explanation":"aqua = a-qua, duae syllabae, non tres.","exerciseType":"multiple-choice","exerciseId":"i-cons-mc","exerciseTitle":"Consonantes: C, G, QU, S, TI","exerciseInstructions":"Elige responsum rectum.","lessonId":"i-consonantes","lessonTitle":"Consonantes","level":"I","lessonUrl":"gradus/fundamenta/consonantes.html"},"cons4":{"id":"cons4","prompt":"Littera 'S' in Latinitate Classica semper sonat:","options":["sine voce (voiceless), ut Anglicum 's' in 'snake'","cum voce (voiced), ut Anglicum 'z' in 'rose', inter vocales","varie, secundum positionem"],"answerIndex":0,"explanation":"S est semper voiceless in Latinitate Classica, differenter ab Anglico.","exerciseType":"multiple-choice","exerciseId":"i-cons-mc","exerciseTitle":"Consonantes: C, G, QU, S, TI","exerciseInstructions":"Elige responsum rectum.","lessonId":"i-consonantes","lessonTitle":"Consonantes","level":"I","lessonUrl":"gradus/fundamenta/consonantes.html"},"cons5":{"id":"cons5","prompt":"Syllaba '-ti-' + vocalis (ut in 'nātiō') pronuntiatur:","options":["[ti], sicut scribitur","[tsi], ut in pronuntiatione posteriore","[ʃi], ut Anglicum 'sh'"],"answerIndex":0,"explanation":"Nulla mollificatio -ti- in aetate classica.","exerciseType":"multiple-choice","exerciseId":"i-cons-mc","exerciseTitle":"Consonantes: C, G, QU, S, TI","exerciseInstructions":"Elige responsum rectum.","lessonId":"i-consonantes","lessonTitle":"Consonantes","level":"I","lessonUrl":"gradus/fundamenta/consonantes.html"},"cons6":{"id":"cons6","statement":"Consonantes geminatae (ut in 'annus') pronuntiantur exactly ut litterae singulae, sine differentia audibili.","answer":false,"explanation":"Geminatae tenentur longius — differentia clare audibilis est.","exerciseType":"true-false","exerciseId":"i-cons-tf","exerciseTitle":"Verum an Falsum: Consonantes","exerciseInstructions":"Dic utrum quaeque sententia vera sit an falsa.","lessonId":"i-consonantes","lessonTitle":"Consonantes","level":"I","lessonUrl":"gradus/fundamenta/consonantes.html"},"cons7":{"id":"cons7","statement":"'R' Latinum est vibrans, similis Hispanico vel Italico, non Anglico Americano.","answer":true,"explanation":"R Latinum trilled/tapped est, non retroflexum.","exerciseType":"true-false","exerciseId":"i-cons-tf","exerciseTitle":"Verum an Falsum: Consonantes","exerciseInstructions":"Dic utrum quaeque sententia vera sit an falsa.","lessonId":"i-consonantes","lessonTitle":"Consonantes","level":"I","lessonUrl":"gradus/fundamenta/consonantes.html"},"cons8":{"id":"cons8","statement":"'H' in Latinitate Classica semper est spiritus fortissimus, clarissime auditus in omni contextu.","answer":false,"explanation":"H est spiritus levis, et iam apud Romanos ipsos interdum neglectus in sermone rapido.","exerciseType":"true-false","exerciseId":"i-cons-tf","exerciseTitle":"Verum an Falsum: Consonantes","exerciseInstructions":"Dic utrum quaeque sententia vera sit an falsa.","lessonId":"i-consonantes","lessonTitle":"Consonantes","level":"I","lessonUrl":"gradus/fundamenta/consonantes.html"},"cons9":{"id":"cons9","statement":"'X' repraesentat coniunctionem duorum sonorum consonantium, [k] + [s].","answer":true,"explanation":"X = KS, ut in 'rex' [reːks].","exerciseType":"true-false","exerciseId":"i-cons-tf","exerciseTitle":"Verum an Falsum: Consonantes","exerciseInstructions":"Dic utrum quaeque sententia vera sit an falsa.","lessonId":"i-consonantes","lessonTitle":"Consonantes","level":"I","lessonUrl":"gradus/fundamenta/consonantes.html"},"cons10":{"id":"cons10","statement":"'G' ante 'e' vel 'i' (ut in 'gemma', 'agit') mollescit in sonum Anglicum 'j', sicut in Italico hodierno.","answer":false,"explanation":"G semper dura manet in Latinitate Classica; mollificatio est evolutio linguarum Romanicarum posteriorum.","exerciseType":"true-false","exerciseId":"i-cons-tf","exerciseTitle":"Verum an Falsum: Consonantes","exerciseInstructions":"Dic utrum quaeque sententia vera sit an falsa.","lessonId":"i-consonantes","lessonTitle":"Consonantes","level":"I","lessonUrl":"gradus/fundamenta/consonantes.html"},"cons11":{"id":"cons11","pairs":[{"left":"C","right":"semper [k], numquam [s] vel [tʃ] (ut in 'Cicero')"},{"left":"G","right":"semper [g] durum, numquam [dʒ] (ut in 'gemma')"},{"left":"QU","right":